al and vertical contacts: \\(40 + 56 = 96\\).\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{E}\\)", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Calculate the blobs of glue within each layer:**\n\n   - **First layer ($4 \\times 4$):**\n   \n     Each sphere in this layer touches the sphere next to it horizontally and vertically. For a $4 \\times 4$ grid, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Horizontal contacts} = 4 \\times (4 - 1) = 4 \\times 3 = 12\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Vertical contacts} = 4 \\times (4 - 1) = 4 \\times 3 = 12\n     \\]\n     Total internal blobs of glue in the first layer:\n     \\[\n     12 + 12 = 24\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Second layer ($3 \\times 3$):**\n   \n     Each sphere in this layer also touches the sphere next to it horizontally and vertically. For a $3 \\times 3$ grid, we have:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Horizontal contacts} = 3 \\times (3 - 1) = 3 \\times 2 = 6\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Vertical contacts} = 3 \\times (3 - 1) = 3 \\times 2 = 6\n     \\]\n     Total internal blobs of glue in the second layer:\n     \\[\n     6 + 6 = 12\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Third layer ($2 \\times 2$):**\n   \n     For a $2 \\times 2$ grid, the internal blobs of glue will be:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Horizontal contacts} = 2 \\times (2 - 1) = 2 \\times 1 = 2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Vertical contacts} = 2 \\times (2 - 1) = 2 \\times 1 = 2\n     \\]\n     Total internal blobs of glue in the third layer:\n     \\[\n     2 + 2 = 4\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Fourth layer (single sphere):** \n   \n     There are no internal contacts in this layer.\n\n2. **Calculate the blobs of glue between layers:**\n   \n   - **Between the first ($4 \\times 4$) layer and the second ($3 \\times 3$):**\n   \n     Each sphere in the $3 \\times 3$ layer touches 4 spheres in the $4 \\times 4$ layer.\n     \\[\n     3 \\times 3 \\times 4 = 9 \\times 4 = 36\n     \\]\n\n   - **Between the second ($3 \\times 3$) layer and the third ($2 \\times 2$):**\n   \n     Each sphere in the $2 \\times 2$ layer